t@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review certified (83ca81e709e); claimed. Probe confirmed fast-import writes get-mark replies to stdout when --cat-blob-fd is absent (two marks read back via readline, exit 0). Commit f6fe5410a74 on branch fix-collapse-windows: FastImportSession now uses stdout=PIPE with no os.pipe and no pass_fds. New regression test test_streamed_engine_does_not_need_pass_fds wraps Popen to raise \"pass_fds not supported on Windows.\" the way CPython does; it failed before the change and passes after it. All 14 collapse tests pass; lint and typecheck clean. Note: this worktree is based on main, which does not yet contain the separate euhedral-svelte-chimpanzee fix (Gerrit 3413); the two changes touch different functions. make verify running.","timestamp":1794942074820168729},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on f6fe5410a74 exited 0 (default tier 21344 passed, 30 skipped; integration tier 222 passed, 2 skipped). Pushed as Gerrit change 3416 (hashtag rebar-session-3d705fec). Note: main now also contains b45a4b7f8ef (euhedral-svelte-chimpanzee), which touches a different function in reclaim_collapse.py and adds tests to the same test module; Gerrit's rebase-if-necessary handles the merge.","timestamp":1794949822371806300},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 1 (f6fe5410a74) got LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, but gerrit_safe_submit.py could not merge it: a textual conflict in tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py with the euhedral-svelte-chimpanzee fix (b45a4b7f8ef), which appended tests at the same place. I rebased onto Gerrit main and kept both test blocks (main's file plus the one new test); the source change is identical. All 16 collapse tests pass on the rebased tree. Patch set 2 is fe949b52b47; its votes reset, so it waits for fresh LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1794951685591998667},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged: Gerrit 3416 patch set 2 (fe949b52b47, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1) landed on main as 0445db3b624 via gerrit_safe_submit.py.\nWindows evidence: test.yml dispatched on main at 0445db3b624, run 44187054507, job \"sweep (windows)\" 134406285171. None of the 8 tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py failures from run 44141097601 / 44151162728 recur, and test_reclaim_collapse.py is not in any .github/windows-sweep-deselect/ file, so they ran and passed.\nThe job itself is still RED with 2 failures that are not in this module: (1) tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py::test_concurrent_cursor_writes_never_report_a_write_error (\"a concurrent cursor write was silently dropped: ['reconcile_cursor_write_error']\"), which also failed in the earlier scheduled run 44151162728 job 134279570332, so it predates this change; (2) tests/unit/test_crash_guard.py::test_xdist_thread_timeout_names_itself_and_the_test (nested xdist worker \"node down: Not properly terminated\"), which did not fail in 44151162728. Neither test touches reclaim code.\nSo this bug's own defect is fixed, but its third criterion as written (\"the sweep (windows) job passing\") is not met. Leaving the ticket in_progress; not ticking that box. Escalated to the coordinator to decide whether to re-scope that criterion to \"no test_reclaim_collapse.py failure in sweep (windows)\" or to wait for the two other failures to be fixed under their own tickets (majestic-depilatory-beetle).","timestamp":1794958893154907161}],"created_at":1794941401341013401,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0c2d8324-64bb-448e-b7d0-564656ef1a4b","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"11aa-b3fb-f239-4f7a"},{"link_uuid":"9b954ac1-2384-4150-b461-a99192591b9a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"480ce0d6-0ece-4fde-be8b-3fca33ad8883","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a8e9-7fde-db0e-4b31"},{"link_uuid":"b7967d33-6f9a-44f7-a83f-63629c0f1cad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b297-24ed-72d7-4dac"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nRun 44141097601 on main at 83ca81e709e: job `sweep (windows)` 134243804938 has 8 failures, all in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py`. Each fails with `AssertionError: pass_fds not supported on Windows.`, raised from `subprocess.Popen` in `FastImportSession.__init__` (`src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse_stream.py`). These are the only failures in that job, and they block `majestic-depilatory-beetle`, whose last acceptance criterion needs the job green.\n\nThe failing tests are `test_apply_collapses_below_horizon_history_and_preserves_reduced_state`, `test_cli_dry_run_reports_plan_without_updating_head`, `test_enforce_since_reanchor_makes_verify_authorship_clean`, `test_fast_import_preserves_metadata_timezone_and_raw_message_bytes`, `test_rewrites_snapshot_ledger_positions_to_new_checkpoint_sha`, `test_stream_failure_raises_and_leaves_the_branch_unchanged`, `test_streamed_engine_matches_the_rewrite_oracle` and `test_streamed_engine_runs_one_fast_import_and_one_batch_reader`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`FastImportSession` opens an `os.pipe()` and passes its write end to `git fast-import --cat-blob-fd=<fd>` through `pass_fds`, so it can read `get-mark` replies. CPython does not support `pass_fds` on Windows.\n\n## Approach\n\ngit's documentation for `--cat-blob-fd` says responses to `get-mark`, `cat-blob` and `ls` go to stdout when the option is absent. The fix drops the extra pipe and `pass_fds`, starts fast-import with `stdout=subprocess.PIPE`, and reads each 40-hex `get-mark` reply from `proc.stdout`. With `--quiet` and no `progress` commands, nothing else is written to stdout. This uses no OS-specific feature, so no test is skipped or deselected on any platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse_stream.py`: read marks from stdout; drop the pipe and `pass_fds`.\n- `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py`: a regression test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Regression.** A test wraps `subprocess.Popen` in `reclaim_collapse_stream` so it raises `AssertionError(\"pass_fds not supported on Windows.\")` whenever `pass_fds` is non-empty, as CPython does on Windows. It then runs a collapse that replays commits and asserts it succeeds. The test fails on the current code and passes with the fix.\n- **Existing tests.** Every test in the module still passes, including the streamed-engine oracle and cost tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `FastImportSession` starts fast-import without `pass_fds` and reads `get-mark` replies from stdout. The new regression test fails before the change and passes after it.\n- [ ] Every test in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py` passes; `make verify` is run and any failure is fixed or shown environmental; the Gerrit change gets `Verified +1`.\n- [ ] After the merge, a `test.yml` run on main shows the `sweep (windows)` job passing; the run and job IDs are recorded on this ticket.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse_stream.py","reason":"Read get-mark replies from fast-import stdout; drop the extra pipe and pass_fds."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"Regression test that rejects pass_fds the way CPython does on Windows."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","6798-606d-37dc-46e7"],["relates_to","a8e9-7fde-db0e-4b31"],["relates_to","b297-24ed-72d7-4dac"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"30401765-803b-4fbe-a85e-bc689a7f7d38","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"567b-e8a3-7db6-4404","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Streamed reclaim collapse fails on Windows: FastImportSession passes pass_fds to Popen","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a9e89e31-8a01-4066-9374-b075f0a35ba7","0c2d8324-64bb-448e-b7d0-564656ef1a4b","9b954ac1-2384-4150-b461-a99192591b9a","b392db6c-afd8-4fd0-80da-22c941e8a0c7","3950bdc7-30e2-4d53-b647-c15156727898","30401765-803b-4fbe-a85e-bc689a7f7d38","16107249-e419-44fe-bbc3-b78634f0d248","20bc1473-e34d-4c04-9d39-48f458a548b0","a660a601-0214-4ee9-953d-9252578dc1f4","480ce0d6-0ece-4fde-be8b-3fca33ad8883","51a58e7f-763b-4083-94df-3273bbb31073","b7967d33-6f9a-44f7-a83f-63629c0f1cad","adf5d53c-a76e-43e7-8df4-50e75c1761aa"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794958893154907162,"uuid":"85b28877-ccd1-4055-aa39-7d4ee57c7b6b"}
